INT. PENGUIN HOUSE - ZOO - MORNING

A glass-walled enclosure of artificial ice and real fish smell. Six keepers in waders jostle around a bucket of herring. The penguins watch from a rock like a jury.

TIMOTHY "TIMBO" OKAFOR (40s, head keeper) hands out gloves. His assistant PRUDHOMME LAVOIE (30s, clipboard) counts birds. Trainee GRETA SOLBERG (20s, notebook) takes notes. Veterinarian DR. ANAND BHATT (50s, stethoscope) squints at a limping bird. Cleaner BEATA KWIATKOWSKA (60s, mop, headphones) hums. Intern WILFRED PARRY (19, enormous boots) holds the bucket upside down.

TIMBO
Wilfred, the bucket.

WILFRED
Sorry, Timbo.

He rights it. Herring slides across the floor. Three penguins launch themselves after it.

PRUDHOMME
That's thirty-one.

GRETA
Thirty-two.

PRUDHOMME
Thirty-one.

ANAND
Thirty, plus the one on Beata's boot.

Beata looks down. A penguin stands on her boot, staring up. She lifts her headphones, nods to it, puts them back, and goes on mopping.

TIMBO
Dr. Bhatt, the limp?

ANAND
It's a sulk.

TIMBO
A sulk?

ANAND
He wants the rock the other one has.

GRETA
(writing)
Sulk. Rock. Other one.

They all look at the rock. A fat penguin sits on it, smug, wings folded behind it like an old man at a bus stop.

WILFRED
I'll swap them.

TIMBO
No!

Too late. Wilfred wades in. Penguins scatter. The sulker slips onto the rock. The fat one slides off and lands on Wilfred's boot. Everyone sighs.

FADE OUT.
